{{!-- "Because of what Stonetop has built" — the seasonal turnover, assembled.

      This is the heaviest thing the sheet is asked to do and the place it used to help least: every
      improvement the steading owns had to be re-read looking for a clause that fires this season,
      and then every rating edited by hand. The list is written from the improvements' own structured
      results, and applying it is one act.

      What is LEFT here, now that most of a season is shown where it happens: the clauses the sheet can
      only state, and the moves a season hands the table. The batch that writes what the season still
      owes went with the bills — the upkeep is what it writes.

      Params: turnover (TurnoverSnapshot). --}}
<div class="steading-turnover">

	{{#if turnover.hasOwnClauses}}
		{{#if turnover.applied}}
			{{!-- Already written. Still shown — what the season did is worth reading after the fact —
			      but with nothing left to press. --}}
			<p class="steading-turnover-applied">{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.alreadyApplied"}}</p>
		{{/if}}
		{{!-- What the season owes that its own steps do not already show: `owed` and `advisoryOwed`
		      leave out the results collected against a step, against the roll they wait on, and in the
		      upkeep — a result stated in both places is the wall this was rebuilt to remove. The Apply
		      below still writes all of them, and its totals still count them. --}}
		{{!-- With the clause. What is left in this list is what no step of the season claimed, so
		      there is nothing above a row here that has stated its trigger — and these are the
		      clauses the sheet cannot judge, which is exactly what the book's own wording says. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-statement" statement=turnover.statement
		    automaticLines=turnover.statement.owed advisoryLines=turnover.statement.advisoryOwed
		    moveSlugs=turnover.statement.grantedMoveSlugs showSource=true showDelta=true
		    showPhrase=true}}
	{{else if turnover.hasClauses}}
		{{!-- Everything this season brings is shown where it happens — in the step it bends, the result
		      row it waits on, the step that generates it, the bills above. Nothing to add here, and a
		      heading over an empty list would read as a section that failed to load. --}}
	{{else}}
		{{!-- Not an error and not an empty state to apologise for: a season in which nothing Stonetop
		      has built fires is an ordinary season. --}}
		<p class="steading-turnover-empty">{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.turnoverEmpty"}}</p>
	{{/if}}

</div>
